# Root .gitignore for Hero Siege Offline Toolkit & hs-game-sdk

# Game Binaries and Proprietary Assets
*.exe
*.dll
*.win
data.win
*.yytex
*.audiogroup*
*.png
*.ogg
*.wav
*.ttf
*.otf

# Extracted Raw Game Data Dumps
hs-game-sdk/data/
**/data/raw/
**/raw/
**/extracted/

# Decompiler / disassembler artifacts — never committed, see "Legal: No
# Decompiled Code in Any Origin" in AGENTS.md. Names + indices go through
# hs-game-sdk instead; full script/disassembly dumps stay on the researcher's
# machine only.
*.i64
*.idb0
*.idb1
*.til
*.gpr
*.rep/
**/ghidra_projects/
**/UndertaleModTool_Export/
**/decompiled/
**/disassembly/
*.dis

# Python Build, Bytecode & Environments
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# C++ Build Artifacts & Intermediate Files
*.obj
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.idb
bin/
out/
x64/
x86/

# Node / TypeScript / Web Build
node_modules/
ts/dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# IDE & OS Specific Files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Junie agent plans/session files (local planning aid, not project docs)
.junie/

# Claude Code: the shared configuration in .claude/ is committed on purpose --
# hooks, agents and skills are project rules, not personal taste. Only the
# per-machine override file is local. It was previously ignored by one
# contributor's global gitignore, which is not a rule a collaborator inherits.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Worktrees created under .claude/. Now that .claude/ is tracked these show up
# as untracked directories, and `git add -A` would try to embed each one as a
# nested repository.
.claude/worktrees/

# Planning documents, for the same reason. A plan says what someone intends to
# build; it is out of date the moment the thing is built, and then the reader
# has two documents and no way to tell which one describes the software they
# are running. What was actually built is recorded in docs/hub/ and the
# decisions in docs/adr/. Keep the plan on your own machine.
*-plan.md
